      "text" : "We need four club tricks alongside two diamonds, two hearts and the spade ace. Play D3 and win the opening lead in South. Cash CA, playing dummy's C2, then lead a low club and play dummy's C7, conceding this round rather than spending CQ. This safety play secures at least four club tricks even against a 5–0 break; if C7 wins, retain that extra trick and reassess. After a club concession, win the defensive return with an appropriate side-suit stopper. Reach dummy with HK to cash CQ, following low from South, then return to South with HA or SA to cash CK and the established remaining club. If a heart return provides the entry to HK, cash CQ immediately; if it forces HA, preserve HK as the subsequent dummy entry. Preserve these transfers rather than cashing side winners prematurely. Once clubs are established, cash the remaining side winners for nine tricks. Favor this safety line over playing for five club tricks.",
