  "rawCandidate" : "{\"plan\":{\"update\":\"replace\",\"text\":\"We need four club tricks alongside two diamonds, two hearts and the spade ace. Play D3 and win the opening lead in South. Cash CA, playing dummy's C2, then lead a low club and play dummy's C7, conceding this round rather than spending CQ. This safety play secures at least four club tricks even against a 5–0 break; if C7 wins, retain that extra trick and reassess. After a club concession, win the defensive return with an appropriate side-suit stopper. Reach dummy with HK to cash CQ, following low from South, then return to South with HA or SA to cash CK and the established remaining club. If a heart return provides the entry to HK, cash CQ immediately; if it forces HA, preserve HK as the subsequent dummy entry. Preserve these transfers rather than cashing side winners prematurely. Once clubs are established, cash the remaining side winners for nine tricks. Favor this safety line over playing for five club tricks.\"},\"selectedCard\":\"D3\",\"publicReason\":\"Play low to win in South, then establish four club tricks with a safety duck while preserving dummy's heart entry.\"}",
  "rawReview" : "{\n  \"verdict\": \"revise\",\n  \"blockingFindings\": [\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"The prescribed club duck does not secure four club tricks against a 5–0 break.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Suppose West holds CJT953 and East is void. West can play C3 under CA, beat dummy's C7 with C9, play C5 under CQ, and retain CJT against South's CK8. Clubs then yield only three tricks. In this same sequence, playing CQ over West's C9 instead, then leading C7 and playing South's C8, forces another high club; CK and C6 subsequently supply the fourth club trick.\",\n      \"requestedChange\": \"Replace the automatic C7 duck and unconditional four-trick guarantee with a complete conditional club plan that responds to the revealed break and West's second-round card. Explain any remaining risk to nine tricks and preserve the entries required by the revised continuation.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"advisorySuggestions\": [\n    \"D3 is legal and consistent with winning the opening lead in South.\"\n  ]\n}",
